# The archive stamp (Issue #68, ADR-0034): git archive, which GitHub uses for every source tarball and
# npm downloads for a github: install, replaces the $Format:...$ placeholders in this one file with the
# commit and its nearest release tag. A checkout keeps the placeholders and reads git itself.
.workstation-archive export-subst
# Vendored third-party code (#472) is checked out byte for byte, never with line endings converted:
# test/vendor.test.js requires it to equal the audited npm package, and the Windows runners check out
# with core.autocrlf=true (read from the tests run on PR #505, which turned LICENSE into CRLF).
src/vendor/** -text
